  "title": "Images keep their edges—and find their cache",
  "summary": "June made image and text requests more useful while giving the growing collection of community projects a clearer home.\n\nGPT Image added transparent PNG output and a `transparent=true` option for generation and editing. Identical simultaneous requests now share a generation, and semantic caching can reuse results for similar prompts.\n\nThe text lineup gained DeepSeek R1-0528, search-enhanced models, and o3 with image input. The `llama` alias moved to Llama 4 Scout, `/models` became easier to browse, and requests without a selected model now use `openai-fast`.\n\nThe project directory gained seven categories and clearer links, then filled out with creative tools, Roblox games, developer wrappers, and CraftUI as the first Vibe Coding entry. Duplicate listings and broken links got some attention too.\n\nChat ads stopped replacing answers, began respecting the authenticated ad preference, and stayed out of JSON responses. Queue changes gave most token-authenticated requests more room, while token validation was reduced from three user-detail queries to one.",
